 "final_text": "The file `/work/putnam_2002_b5.lean` now compiles with no errors and no `sorry` warning. The only output is linter warnings: a deprecation notice for `push_neg` and an unused `omega` after `norm_num`.\n\nThe proof uses an explicit construction. Let M = 2002! \u00b7 2\u00b710\u00b9\u2070 and n = M\u00b2. For each j in 1..2002, write M/j = b+1. Then n = j\u00b2(b+1)\u00b2 = j\u00b2 + b\u00b7(2j\u00b2 + b\u00b7j\u00b2), so n has base-b digits [j\u00b2, 2j\u00b2, j\u00b2], which is a palindrome of length 3 whenever b > 2j\u00b2. The map j \u21a6 b = M/j \u2212 1 is injective on 1..2002, which gives at least 2002 bases. A finiteness argument is needed for `ncard`: any base b > M\u00b2 would make n a one-digit number, so the set sits inside `Iic (M\u00b2)`.",
